# The Visible Focus Indicator

Browsers show a focus outline (often a blue ring) when an element is focused. Never remove it with `outline: none` unless you provide a custom, clearly visible alternative.

Good practice:
```css
:focus {
  outline: 3px solid #4A90E2;
  outline-offset: 2px;
}
```
Focus styles help keyboard users see where they are.
